            <ArticleTitle>Short-lived 195mAu for evaluation of left ventricular function by first-pass radionuclide angiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>191-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 52 patients with coronary artery disease the feasibility of performing first-pass cardiac studies with the short-lived tracer 195mAu was tested. Even with a currently available gamma camera, good results were obtained in terms of imaging quality, reproducibility and exercise response. The use of a multicrystal camera would, however, be desirable.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
